    <task id="LOCAL-00006" summary="Fixed the most deceptive bug I've ever encountered. The symptom was that (rule in model) was False, even though the rule's condition was in the model's population dictionary. This issue is caused when the keys to a dictionary are mutated from an outside source, and they cause the keys in the dict to be associated with outdated hash values. In this particular case the mutation was literally caused by the mutation operator in the GA component of the LCS. The fix is to copy conditions before mutating them.">
